course: dictionary
lesson: 11359
title: Zoom: fast, bigger, or rising
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Zoom has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to pick. Look at the words near it. «The Road Runner zooms off in a cloud of dust» means zoom is about speed, because the dust and the word off show something moving away fast.
explain: Zoom can also be about pictures. «Zoom in» makes a picture look bigger and closer, and «zoom out» makes it look smaller and farther away. When a sentence mentions a screen, a camera or a map, check whether the picture is changing size.
explain: Zoom can also mean rising very quickly, like prices or numbers. If a sentence talks about numbers and says zoom up, think: going up fast. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Zoom is a verb: zoom, zooms, zoomed, zooming. It is also a noun: a zoom, or a zoom lens on a camera.
fact: To zoom means to move very fast, often with a buzzing or roaring sound.
fact: «Zoom in» means make a picture look bigger and closer; «zoom out» means make it look smaller and farther away.
fact: To zoom up means to rise very quickly, like prices or numbers.
fact: Zoom is also the name of a video-call app.
exercise: «The Road Runner zooms off in a cloud of dust.» What does zooms mean here? | Stops suddenly | Makes a picture look bigger | Rises slowly like a balloon | *Moves very fast
exercise: Jayden says «zoom in» makes a picture look smaller. What is the right meaning? | It makes the picture go dark | It makes the picture look smaller and farther away | It turns the camera off | *It makes the picture look bigger and closer
exercise: «Numbers zoom up when they grow fast.» What does zoom up mean? | *Rise very quickly | Fall slowly | Turn into words | Stay exactly the same
test: Find and copy the phrase that means make a picture look smaller and farther away. | *zoom out | zoom in | zoom past | zoom off
test: «Sonic zooms round loops faster than sound.» Which meaning fits best? | *Moves very fast | Rises very quickly like prices | Stops for a rest | Makes a picture look smaller
exam: «Zoomed right out, you see the whole world with little detail.» What is this describing? | A picture made bigger, so you see every river bend | A video call with friends | *A picture made smaller, so you see the whole world | A fast car on a busy road
